{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "UML Object Diagrams"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about object diagrams."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Build the macrosystem conceptual model following the customer requirements, through the use and interpretation of collected information, represented in class diagrams, interaction diagrams, and operation contracts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Recognizes basic ideas on programming tools, diagrams of cases, and data flow diagrams."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information about UML object diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Pick a specific situation in which you need to organize data in a diagram (like in Sarah's case). Think about your needs: Do you want to include all information? What kind of information do you need? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Organize your data in a diagram according to your needs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share it with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for more information about UML object diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I think about particular needs when organizing data in diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I organize data in a diagram according to those needs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my results with my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Want to in Negative Statements with Adverbs of Frequency"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the verb <span class=\"strong\">want to </span>plus another verb to express wishes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">want to in negative statements </span>to express that you do not wish that something happens. In order to create these type of sentences, follow the next structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <span class=\"strong\">do not (don't) </span>/ <span class=\"strong\">does not (doesn't) </span>+ <span class=\"strong\">want to </span>+ verb + complement</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">don't want to </span>include too much information on the diagram. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Frequency</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can complement the previous sentences by expressing the frequency in which you <span class=\"strong\">don't want </span>something to happen. These are <span class=\"strong\">adverbs of frequency </span>that you can use for these statements:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb of Frequency\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> usually don't want to </span> create new diagrams. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Often\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> She <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> often doesn't want to </span> read about diagrams. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sometimes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> sometimes don't want to </span> have everything under one class.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I usually don't want to overload my system with a bunch of data that I don't need."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My customers sometimes don't want to provide certain information. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Pronouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">subject </span>and <span class=\"strong\">object pronouns </span>to replace subject or objects within a statement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">subject pronouns </span>when we want to reduce proper and common nouns repetition within statements. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The following charts shows you what the <span class=\"strong\">subject </span>and <span class=\"strong\">object pronouns </span>are: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject Pronouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Object Pronouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Me\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Him\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Us \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Them \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's see how we can use <span class=\"strong\">subject pronouns </span>to avoid repetition by comparing these two group of sentences:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">The engineer </span>designs a new software. <span class=\"strong\">The engineer </span>needs to visualize the data so, <span class=\"strong\">the engineer </span>uses a diagram. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">The engineer </span>designs a new software. <span class=\"strong\">He </span>needs to visualize the data so, <span class=\"strong\">he </span>uses a diagram. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, let's see how we can use <span class=\"strong\">object pronouns </span>to avoid repetition by comparing these two group of sentences:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The engineer designs a new software for <span class=\"strong\">his boss</span>. He really wants to impress<span class=\"strong\">his boss</span> .  </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The engineer designs a new software for<span class=\"strong\">his boss</span>. He really wants to impress <span class=\"strong\">him</span>.  </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I just need to create an object diagram. It will help you to have not only general but also detailed information about them."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Object diagrams help us visualize one instance of time and all the data that the system has in that specific moment. They are common to illustrate particular snapshot scenarios. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "instance "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "example of a situation"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Object diagrams help us visualize one instance of time and all the data that the system has in that specific moment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "snapshot "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "image of the current status of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are common to illustrate particular snapshot scenarios."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "instance specification"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "instance you describe with proper detail"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They look similar to class diagrams but they don't need to have an instance specification."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "visualize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to see; observe"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Object diagrams help us visualize one instance of time and all the data that the system has in that specific moment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overload "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put an extra load on something and exceed its capacity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I usually don't want to overload my system with a bunch of data that I don't need."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sarah:</span> Hey, Josh. I need your help. As you know, I collected important data about my customers; So, I need you to create a mechanism that helps me organize that data. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Josh:</span> Sure, Sarah. I just need to create an object diagram. It will help you to have not only general but also detailed information about them. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sarah:</span> What exactly can I see on an object diagram? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Josh:</span> Well, object diagrams help us visualize one instance of time and all the data that the system has in that specific moment. They are common to illustrate particular snapshot scenarios. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sarah:</span> That sounds great. But, I usually don't want to overload my system with a bunch of data that I don't need. Also, my customers sometimes don't want to provide certain information. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Josh:</span> That's not an issue. Object diagrams are very useful; they look similar to class diagrams but they don't need to have an instance specification."}, {"time": "57500", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sarah:</span> What kind of elements do we need to include in an object diagram? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Josh:</span> First, you need an object name and class name to describe the elements on the diagram. For instance, the object name of your diagram could be \u201cMyFrequentCustomers\u201d and the class name could be \u201cCustomers\u201d.  <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sarah:</span> Is that it? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Josh:</span> Not really, we also need to include attributes and their values. The names of the customers could be the attributes and their contact information, the values."}, {"time": "88000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sarah:</span> And, what if I don't have the customer's name but I have his contact information? , or what if I don't want to include certain data into the object diagram? Can I do that? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Josh:</span> Definitely! That is what we call suppressing elements. We can suppress some attributes, or all of them if we want to. We can even suppress the object name. The diagram will only show us what we want to see."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say what object diagrams help visualize. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the elements that appear in an object diagram."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss how to suppress elements in an object diagram."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are diagrams useful for?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What information do you usually include in a diagram?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Design and D